cadtui localisation — data-file schema + loader/converter (P2)

Parent: cadtui.issue (Phase 7, localisation). cadtui has two localisable
vocabularies (interaction-language verbs/keywords, which WE author, and the CAD
command vocabulary, which must be MEASURED on localised CAD installs — see the
sibling probe issues). This ticket defines the data format all locale
dictionaries take (data, NOT code — spec §Localisation) and the loader.

Goal
- Per-locale sexp data files under clautolisp/cadtui/data/locale/<locale>/ :
  - commands.sexp        — alist (international-name . local-name) for CAD
                           command names (AutoCAD-style: international English is
                           canonical, `_`-prefix forces it; getcname is the
                           source of truth).
  - option-keywords.sexp — alist ((command . international-keyword)
                           . (local-keyword . local-abbrev)).
  - aliases.sexp         — alist (keyboard-alias . command) from acad.pgp /
                           default.pgp (purely local, never `_`-prefixed).
  These are three DISTINCT dictionaries with different prefixing rules; never
  merge them (spec "Trois dictionnaires distincts").
- A loader in the (future) cadtui localisation layer: local-name /
  international-name do a bidirectional lookup; ANY missing entry falls back to
  the international form so partial data never fails (spec lines ~744-746).
- The interaction-language dictionary (verbs + meta-command keywords) is
  authored by us (fr_FR first), same sexp shape, under the same tree.

Converter
- Raw probe artifacts land under dist/getcname/ etc. (see probe issues). A
  converter script (mirror scripts/classify-sysvar-diff.py) turns a reviewed
  artifact into the committed sexp. getcname output is generated fact (safe to
  import); bulk-copied vendor doc tables are NOT — verify per case.

Notes
- The interaction-language parser stays in canonical ENGLISH tokens; localisation
  is a lexical pre-pass BEFORE parsing, never a grammar duplicated per language.
- This ticket is headless (schema + loader + converter + fr_FR interaction
  dictionary). The CAD-command DATA depends on the probe issues below.
